# uv, ninja and git from flake.nix; without nix, they have to be on PATH already.
# Either way the C++ compiler is the host's (see flake.nix for why).
if has nix; then
  use flake
fi

# uv project: sync (fast when up to date; again whenever uv.lock or
# pyproject.toml change) and activate .venv, for the shell and nvim alike.
# Every dependency group: tests, lint, editor tooling (ruff, ty) and the
# benchmark commands. A plain `uv run` afterwards leaves them installed.
layout uv --all-groups
